<title>USA: NCR Corp to buy back odd lot shares.</title>
<headline>NCR Corp to buy back odd lot shares.</headline>
<dateline>DAYTON, Ohio 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>NCR Corp said on Thursday that it is offering to purchase common shares from holders of less than 100 shares of NCR's common stock.</p>
<p>The expiration for the offer unless extended is July 31, 1997 at 1700 EDT, NCR said.</p>
<p>The offer price is based on the prices of program transactions on five trading days after The First National Bank of Boston receives instructions from the investor or the investor's broker, NCR said.</p>
<p>The voluntary program is being offered to provide a low cost means for odd-lot shareowners to liquidate their holdings, NCR said.</p>
</text>
